  "limitations": [
    "Both S5 versions were derived after reading aggregate results from the full PPT period. The temporal split is diagnostic, not an independent holdout.",
    "S5-v0.2 was introduced after the literal entry-first S5-v0.1 showed large unconfirmed losses, so its comparison is iterative research rather than pre-registered evidence.",
    "The PPT did not define a one-contract portfolio. First confirmation and volume are deterministic execution tie-breakers.",
    "OHLC touches are converted to next-actual-bar execution with slippage, commission, and 10% volume participation.",
    "No LSMA, moving average, VIX, or futures direction is used."
  ]
